rota lap 4330, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. Its threshold asks the lap to listen rather
rota than scan: the claim a page keeps repeating, the question it keeps answering, and the silence
rota where a claim used to be and a witness now stands. Its dual seat, the grain, carries the ear's
rota hard rule out loud -- a guard that cannot red guards nothing, so a witness must be proven able
rota to make a sound before its silence means anything. That sentence chose the lap.

think Listening for a silence, I read the head of construction/standing-equipment.kyri, which
think quotes that very strand and then says: "every guard here can red." That is a claim about 260
think rows, and nothing in the tree counts it.
think Measured by grep over every rostered path: 199 of 260 reach a prove-red mode, a control
think fixture, or a plant; 61 do not. A grep is a proxy, so I narrowed it honestly -- a code
think witness that runs a program and asserts on its output is red-capable by construction, where
think a tree scan compared against a ceiling is not. Of the 61, twelve invoke a tree scan, and two
think of the twelve have a control.
think The loudest of the ten is tools/fixtures/s/sow_leak_scan.sh -- the wall between the
think maintainer's own name and a repository built to carry none. sow runs it every cadence lap;
think it has answered IDENT_CLEAN every time; nothing had ever planted a name in front of it. Its
think one demonstrated red was a FALSE one: REDS %244, when a blanket history rewrite turned two of
think its own entries into the public pseudonym and 22 projected files failed a privacy check about
think nothing. A guard whose only demonstrated red was wrong is the guard whose green is worth least.

obs Wrote tools/fixtures/s/sow_leak_control.sh: seven gated legs, each running the scan with its
obs working directory inside a throwaway pen holding a seed/ of its own, so the real seed/ is never
obs touched and custody gate %1 is nowhere near it. Planted name reads IDENT_LEAK and names its
obs file; a lowercase spelling is caught, which checks the scan's own -i claim; a bracketed entry
obs catches its plain spelling, which is %244's repair; a contact identifier is caught; clean prose
obs and the .sow-withheld.log exclusion walk free.
obs Shown from the failing side twice, since a refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot
obs be told from a bypass. Dropping -i from a copy of the scan fails leg 3; removing the bracketed
obs entry fails leg 4; lifting each plant returns control_verdict=ok. SOW_LEAK_SCAN points the
obs control at the copy, which is how the plants are shown to land.
obs Two readings are REPORTED rather than gated, because each describes the instrument truly and a
obs wall at zero would misdescribe it: a name inside a binary file is invisible to the scan's -I,
obs and an ABSENT seed/ reads IDENT_CLEAN -- a clean answer about a corpus that is not there. The
obs second is held by ORDERING rather than by the scan: sow_witness duty 2 projects fresh and
obs asserts SOW_OK before duty 3 reads anything. That sentence is now written into the witness,
obs because moving duty 3 ahead of duty 2 would turn it green over an empty directory.
obs Seated as duty 0 of tools/s/sow_witness.rish, ahead of the four duties that read the seed,
obs since those four prove a clean seed only if the scan could have said otherwise.

obs THE INSTRUMENT EARNED ITS KEEP INSIDE THE HOUR. A standing seed_link red was waiting on the
obs cold pass: README.md -> context/BHAKTA_STYLE.md, a front door linking into a room the seed does
obs not carry. The Bhakta register was seated at 12:09 today and template-manifest.bron never
obs learned it, while its four siblings -- RADIANT, TWILIGHT, GAUGE, CIVIC -- all ship under the
obs same scrub verdict. I asked the new control before proposing the line: the page reads
obs IDENT_LEAK in the field, exactly as RADIANT_STYLE.md does, which carries the name four times in
obs the field and zero in the seed. The scrub is what handles it, so the line is safe. Seated
obs allow context/BHAKTA_STYLE.md. This is a claim across lanes -- the register is petrichor's and
obs incense's room -- named here and on the day shelf for their review.

obs AGAINST MYSELF, THREE TIMES. First, the lap opened onto an orphaned --scoped pass holding the
obs runner's lock, whose parent had exited; the runner named it and named the repair, and TERM
obs released it, yet the release is not instant and my immediate relaunch was refused against a pid
obs already dying. Second, I ran sow_witness by hand beside my own cold pass, so a projection
obs rebuilt seed/ underneath it -- sow_lock red is mine, and it is REDS %193 exactly. Third and
obs worst, I read seed_link red in the same window and wrote it off as the same race; re-run over a
obs complete projection it reds identically, so a real red on the front door was one inference away
obs from being buried under my own noise. I also edited the tree mid-pass, so the cold close reads
obs tree_moved; the --hot pass is the gating read.

obs A READER TAKES NO LOCK. %193 serialized the WRITERS of seed/. tools/fixtures/s/seed_link_scan.sh
obs reads that directory with no lock and no ordering relationship to any projection, and it runs at
obs tier lap. sow_lock_witness's own head names three readers of the public face -- sow_leak_scan,
obs sow_witness, publish-seed -- and misses the one with no ordering protection at all. Named for
obs Keaton rather than taken, since a reader taking the projection lock changes a custody-adjacent
obs guard.

obs FOR THE FLEET, DESIGN RATHER THAN FAULT. The runner prints "evidence <path>" at the moment of a
obs red and lands the file at the CLOSE, clearing the elder room first -- deliberately, since a file
obs written mid-run would move the tree digest it sits beside. So a hand reading a red while the pass
obs runs finds that path absent, or holding a KILLED pass's copy. Two ships met that today and read
obs it as a fault.

